    <profile id="ab7788d0-91c6-9250-06b8-b07f82536675-800b0" name="Cluster Mine" page="0" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">After your army deploys, Scouts redeploy and lnfiltrators deploy, but before the roll to Seize the Initiative, each unit with cluster mines in your army may booby-trap a single piece of battlefield terrain on the table. The piece of battlefield terrain should be marked with a small marker to remind both players that it has been booby-trapped. Enemy models treat booby-trapped pieces of battlefield terrain as dangerous terrain. Note that having multiple units booby-trap the same piece of area terrain has no additional effect. A unit with cluster mines which begins the game in Reserve may still booby-trap a piece of battlefield terrain.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile id="fed1624b-0543-fad6-1691-d239f3e09687-800b0" name="Combat Shield" page="0" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82">
